  "steps": [
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "short": "Logged in",
      "title": "Alice logs in",
      "chapter": "setup",
      "body": "Alice signs in and adds two things to her cart. Her request happened to land on Server A, which keeps a [[session]] in its memory: who she is and what’s in her cart.\n\nHer browser holds a cookie with the session id, so later requests can find it again.",
      "callout": {
        "kind": "insight",
        "text": "**State** is anything a server remembers between requests: logins, carts, half-finished uploads."
      },
      "changes": [],
      "metrics": {
        "ok": "1 / 1",
        "extra": "+0 ms"
      },
      "overrides": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "short": "Logged out",
      "title": "Her next request lands elsewhere",
      "chapter": "problem",
      "body": "The load balancer is doing its job — round robin sends Alice’s next requests to B and then C. Neither has ever heard of her.\n\nTo Alice the app is broken: one page shows her cart, the next asks her to sign in again.",
      "callout": {
        "kind": "warning",
        "text": "If a server keeps state in memory, every other server is useless for that user."
      },
      "changes": [
        "~ Requests 2 and 3 go to B and C",
        "- “Please sign in again”"
      ],
      "metrics": {
        "ok": "1 / 3",
        "survive": "no",
        "scale": "no",
        "extra": "+0 ms"
      },
      "overrides": {
        "b": {
          "visible": false
        },
        "c": {
          "visible": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "short": "Sticky",
      "title": "Fix 1: sticky sessions",
      "chapter": "solution",
      "body": "Tell the load balancer to remember where each user started — usually with a cookie — and keep sending them there. Alice always reaches A, so she stays signed in.\n\nQuick to switch on, and no code changes.",
      "callout": {
        "kind": "warning",
        "text": "Sticky users can’t be moved. If many of them pile onto one server, it stays overloaded while others idle."
      },
      "changes": [
        "~ LB pins Alice → Server A",
        "~ All her requests succeed"
      ],
      "metrics": {
        "ok": "3 / 3",
        "survive": "no",
        "scale": "limited",
        "extra": "+0 ms"
      },
      "overrides": {
        "lb-2": {
          "visible": false
        },
        "b": {
          "emphasis": true
        },
        "b-2": {
          "visible": false
        },
        "c": {
          "emphasis": true
        },
        "ul-2": {
          "visible": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "short": "A dies",
      "title": "…until Server A dies",
      "chapter": "problem",
      "body": "Server A crashes. The load balancer does the right thing and moves Alice to B — but her session died with A’s memory.\n\nShe’s signed out and her cart is empty. Every user pinned to A just had the same experience.",
      "callout": {
        "kind": "warning",
        "text": "Sticky sessions turn every server into a small single point of failure for its users."
      },
      "changes": [
        "- Server A down",
        "- Alice’s session lost",
        "~ Cart 2 items → empty"
      ],
      "metrics": {
        "ok": "0 / 3",
        "survive": "no",
        "scale": "limited",
        "extra": "+0 ms"
      },
      "overrides": {
        "alice": {
          "visible": false
        },
        "lb-2": {
          "visible": false
        },
        "b-2": {
          "emphasis": true
        },
        "ul-2": {
          "visible": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "short": "Shared store",
      "title": "Fix 2: move the state out",
      "chapter": "solution",
      "body": "Keep sessions in a shared, fast [[session store]] (often Redis). Every server reads Alice’s session from it, so any server can handle any request.\n\nThe servers are now [[stateless]]: they remember nothing between requests. Round robin is back, and she stays signed in.",
      "callout": {
        "kind": "tip",
        "text": "The cost: one extra hop of about a millisecond per request — cheap, for servers you can add, remove or lose freely."
      },
      "changes": [
        "+ Session store",
        "~ Servers keep nothing in memory",
        "~ Round robin again"
      ],
      "metrics": {
        "ok": "3 / 3",
        "survive": "yes",
        "scale": "yes",
        "extra": "+1 ms"
      },
      "overrides": {
        "alice": {
          "emphasis": true
        },
        "lb-2": {
          "emphasis": true
        },
        "a-2": {
          "visible": false
        },
        "ul-2": {
          "emphasis": true
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s6",
      "short": "Lose one",
      "title": "Now losing a server is a non-event",
      "chapter": "insight",
      "body": "Server A dies again. The load balancer routes around it, B and C read the same session from the store, and Alice doesn’t notice.\n\nThis is what makes autoscaling possible: servers can be created and destroyed at any moment.",
      "callout": {
        "kind": "insight",
        "text": "Stateless servers are cattle, not pets — any one of them can be replaced without anyone noticing."
      },
      "changes": [
        "- Server A down",
        "~ Alice still signed in, cart intact"
      ],
      "metrics": {
        "ok": "3 / 3",
        "survive": "yes",
        "scale": "yes",
        "extra": "+1 ms"
      },
      "overrides": {
        "a-2": {
          "emphasis": true
        },
        "a-3": {
          "visible": false
        },
        "la-5": {
          "visible": false
        },
        "as": {
          "visible": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s7",
      "short": "Tokens",
      "title": "Or: let the request carry it",
      "chapter": "technique",
      "body": "Another option is to put the state in the request itself: a signed [[token]] (such as a JWT) that says “this is Alice”. Any server can verify the signature without looking anything up.\n\nNo store and no extra hop — but a token can’t easily be cancelled before it expires, and it travels with every request, so keep it small.",
      "callout": {
        "kind": "tip",
        "text": "Common split: tokens for identity, a shared store for anything big or that must change instantly (carts, revoked logins)."
      },
      "changes": [
        "- Session store",
        "+ Signed token in each request",
        "~ Extra hop gone"
      ],
      "metrics": {
        "ok": "3 / 3",
        "survive": "yes",
        "scale": "yes",
        "extra": "+0 ms"
      },
      "overrides": {
        "alice": {
          "visible": false
        },
        "a-3": {
          "emphasis": true
        },
        "st": {
          "visible": false
        },
        "ul-2": {
          "visible": false
        },
        "la-5": {
          "emphasis": true
        },
        "as": {
          "visible": false
        },
        "bs": {
          "visible": false
        },
        "cs": {
          "visible": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s8",
      "short": "Uploads",
      "title": "Case: files on a local disk",
      "chapter": "problem",
      "body": "Alice uploads a new avatar. Server A saves `avatar.png` to its own disk and shows it — perfect.\n\nHer next page loads from Server B, which has no such file: a broken image. Files are state too.",
      "callout": {
        "kind": "warning",
        "text": "Anything written to a server’s local disk — uploads, generated PDFs, temp files — disappears for every other server, and for good when the server is replaced."
      },
      "changes": [
        "+ Avatar saved on Server A’s disk",
        "- Broken image when served by B or C"
      ],
      "metrics": {
        "ok": "1 / 3",
        "survive": "no",
        "scale": "no",
        "extra": "+0 ms"
      },
      "overrides": {
        "alice": {
          "visible": false
        },
        "a-3": {
          "visible": false
        },
        "b-3": {
          "visible": false
        },
        "c-3": {
          "visible": false
        },
        "st": {
          "visible": false
        },
        "ul-2": {
          "visible": false
        },
        "la-5": {
          "visible": false
        },
        "lbb-5": {
          "visible": false
        },
        "lc-5": {
          "visible": false
        },
        "as": {
          "visible": false
        },
        "bs": {
          "visible": false
        },
        "cs": {
          "visible": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s9",
      "short": "Object store",
      "title": "Put files in object storage",
      "chapter": "solution",
      "body": "Store files in shared [[object storage]] (Amazon S3, Google Cloud Storage, Azure Blob): effectively unlimited, durable, and reachable from every server.\n\nServer A writes the avatar there (dark square); B and C read the same file. Better still, browsers fetch images straight from storage through a CDN.",
      "callout": {
        "kind": "tip",
        "text": "Rule of thumb: servers keep nothing that must outlive the request. Sessions → a store or token; files → object storage; data → the database."
      },
      "changes": [
        "+ Object storage",
        "~ Uploads written to storage, not local disk",
        "~ Every server sees every file"
      ],
      "metrics": {
        "ok": "3 / 3",
        "survive": "yes",
        "scale": "yes",
        "extra": "+0 ms"
      },
      "overrides": {
        "alice": {
          "visible": false
        },
        "a-3": {
          "emphasis": true
        },
        "b-3": {
          "emphasis": true
        },
        "c-3": {
          "emphasis": true
        },
        "st": {
          "visible": false
        },
        "ul-2": {
          "visible": false
        },
        "la-5": {
          "emphasis": true
        },
        "lbb-5": {
          "emphasis": true
        },
        "lc-5": {
          "emphasis": true
        },
        "as": {
          "visible": false
        },
        "bs": {
          "visible": false
        },
        "cs": {
          "visible": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s10",
      "short": "Recap",
      "title": "Recap",
      "chapter": "recap",
      "body": "• State kept in a server’s memory **pins users** to that server.\n• **Sticky sessions** hide the problem until a server dies.\n• Move state to a **shared store**, or carry it in a **signed token**.\n• Files go to **object storage**, never a server’s local disk.\n• **Stateless** servers can be added, removed and lost freely.",
      "callout": {
        "kind": "tip",
        "text": "Next up: **Caching** — the database behind all these stateless servers is about to become the bottleneck."
      },
